Z||000010||starfighter007@msn.com||08-10-2001||02:23 PM||||Kanada  it does sound like a fuel problem. It may be that your fuel pump is on its way out .Like when it gets hot it can't pump no more.you probobly could check this in your drive way by running it for a while till it warms up then try to drive it out of your driveway it should stall under load.But you will still need a fuel preasure gauge to check this.It could be your fuel filter is clogged or in backwards.It could be a colapsed fuel line.My gut feeling from what you are telling us this fuel pump related.You will need a presure gauge from auto zone to ckeck this.I hope this helps you some what. These are the first steps that I would take to try and find the cause of the problem you are haveing.Hope this helps <p>[This message has been edited by starfighter007@msn.com (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
